    <h2>The honest answer</h2>
    <p><strong>If you are a brand-new business spending under $100/month on marketing, Wix is fine.</strong> Get something live, run the experiment, see if the business sticks. The opportunity cost of a slow site at month 1 is small.</p>
    <p><strong>If you are an established service business spending real money on Google Ads or SEO, Wix is leaving money on the table.</strong> The page-speed gap alone &mdash; the difference between a 60 PageSpeed score and a 95 &mdash; is the difference between visitors bouncing and visitors calling. Over a year, that gap is worth more than the cost of a custom build, several times over.</p>
